Object.assign(window.WIKI_DEMO_DATA.pages,{
"server-information":{title:"Server Information",group:"Server",summary:"How to join Enthusia and what kind of survival server it is.",body:`<p>Enthusia is a permanent semi-anarchy survival world with a player-run economy, guilds, PvP systems, progression, community events and a long-running player history.</p><h2>Joining</h2><div class="fact-grid"><div><b>Java</b><span>enthusia.net</span></div><div><b>Bedrock</b><span>enthusia.net · port 19132</span></div></div><p>Java and Bedrock players share the same SMP. Some menus are presented differently on Bedrock, but the underlying economy, guild, progression and player data is shared.</p><h2>The world</h2><p>The SMP is intended to be permanent rather than a short seasonal reset. Bases, roads, ruins, farms, battle sites, public builds and player projects can become part of the server's history over time.</p><div class="callout"><b>No land claims.</b> Bases are not protected by automatic claim borders. They can be found, raided and griefed under the normal server rules, so location privacy and trust matter.</div><p><a data-page="base-privacy">Base Privacy</a> explains how Enthusia reduces some client-side clues that can otherwise make hidden bases unusually easy to locate. It is not claim protection and it does not make bases impossible to find.</p><h2>PvP</h2><p>PvP and raiding are part of the SMP. The <a data-page="warzone">Warzone</a> has rotating combat rules, while <a data-page="duels">Death Duels</a> are consensual 1v1 fights where players can configure rules and wagers.</p><h2>Economy</h2><p><a data-page="raw-gold">Raw Gold</a> is the server's physical currency. It can be carried as ordinary Raw Gold or Raw Gold Blocks, deposited into a bank balance, withdrawn again, paid to other players and used by integrated systems such as the <a data-page="market">Market</a>.</p><h2>Community</h2><p><a data-page="guilds">Guilds</a> organize player groups. The community side of the wiki records individual <a data-special="players">players</a>, <a data-special="guilds">guilds</a>, builds, mapart and server history separately from the mechanics guides.</p><h2>Useful commands for new players</h2><table><tr><td><code>/rules</code></td><td>Open or display the server rules.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/newbie</code></td><td>Open the new-player information available on the server.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/website</code></td><td>Get the official Enthusia website.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/discord</code></td><td>Get the official Discord link.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/store</code></td><td>Get the official store link.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/spawn</code></td><td>Teleport to spawn after the normal warmup.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/commands</code></td><td>The complete command reference is on this wiki's <a data-page="commands">Commands</a> page.</td></tr></table>`},
"events":{title:"Events",group:"Community",summary:"The event system in development, its commands, and how each implemented event is played.",body:`<div class="status-card"><span class="dot amber"></span><div><b>Server Events — in development</b><p>The custom Server Events system is not enabled on the SMP right now. The information below documents the event system being built so players can see what is planned and how the implemented games work.</p></div></div><div class="status-card"><span class="dot gray"></span><div><b>KOTH</b><p>KOTH is currently disabled.</p></div></div><h2>How Server Events work</h2><p>When enabled, one physical event can run at a time. An event moves through a vote or selection phase, a join period, a ready/countdown period, the game itself, results, and then restoration of each player's normal SMP state.</p><p>Your normal inventory and player state are saved before event gameplay. Event equipment is separate from your normal SMP loadout; after the event, the system restores your inventory, armor, offhand, health, food, experience, game mode, effects, movement state and original location.</p><h3>Event commands</h3><table><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does when Events is enabled</th></tr><tr><td><code>/event</code></td><td>Show the current event and its phase.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/event join</code></td><td>Join the current event while joining is open.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/event leave</code></td><td>Leave the event and restore your saved SMP state.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/event spectate</code></td><td>Spectate the current event when spectating is available.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/event vote</code></td><td>Open the event-voting menu while a vote is active.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/event start</code></td><td>Open the menu of events that can be player-started.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/event start &lt;event&gt;</code></td><td>Attempt to start a specific available event.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/event stats</code></td><td>Open event statistics.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/event next</code></td><td>Show the next scheduled event-vote time. <code>/event time</code> and <code>/event timer</code> are aliases.</td></tr></table><p>While an event is controlling a player, normal escape and economy commands are restricted so players cannot teleport out, bring SMP items into the game, or use event areas as an economy exploit.</p><h2>Combat and elimination events</h2><table><tr><th>Event</th><th>How to play</th></tr><tr><td><b>SkyWars</b></td><td>Start on an island, loot tiered chests, use the available kit/items and eliminate the other players. The last player alive wins. Event terrain can be modified and restored afterward.</td></tr><tr><td><b>BedWars</b></td><td>Protect your team's bed, gather generator resources, buy items and upgrades, and destroy enemy beds. You respawn while your bed survives; once it is gone, your next death is final. The last team alive wins.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Fight 1v1</b></td><td>Direct or bracket-style combat. Defeat the other player to advance/win.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Fight 2v2</b></td><td>Two-player teams fight until one team is eliminated. This mode is implemented but is not currently planned as an enabled selection.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Fight FFA</b></td><td>Every player for themselves; the last surviving player wins.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Sumo 1v1</b></td><td>Knock the opponent off the platform before they knock you off.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Sumo 2v2</b></td><td>Team sumo. Eliminate the opposing team by knocking its players from the platform. This mode is implemented but is not currently planned as an enabled selection.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Sumo FFA</b></td><td>Free-for-all sumo; stay on the platform while knocking everyone else off.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Knockback FFA</b></td><td>Knockback-focused free-for-all elimination. Ender Pearls are specifically allowed by this event type.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Quake</b></td><td>Fast railgun-style combat. Score hits/kills with the event weapon while players respawn and race for the winning score.</td></tr><tr><td><b>One in the Chamber</b></td><td>Projectile combat with limited shots. Land your shots, earn more opportunities and outscore the other players while respawns continue.</td></tr></table><h2>Team objective events</h2><table><tr><th>Event</th><th>How to play</th></tr><tr><td><b>Capture the Flag</b></td><td>Take the enemy team's flag and return it while protecting your own. Flags can be carried, dropped and returned. The implemented win target is three captures.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Capture Players</b></td><td>Capture and carry enemy players into your team's jail/capture area while rescuing imprisoned teammates. The intended setup uses five captures toward a round and three round wins for the match.</td></tr></table><h2>Party and survival events</h2><table><tr><th>Event</th><th>How to play</th></tr><tr><td><b>Block Party</b></td><td>A concrete color is announced. Get onto that color before the other colors disappear. Falling eliminates you.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Hot Potato</b></td><td>A potato is passed between players. Get rid of it before the elimination timer catches you and survive the later rounds.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Spleef</b></td><td>Break the event floor beneath other players while keeping yourself from falling.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Splegg</b></td><td>Projectile-based Spleef: fire to destroy floor blocks and make other players fall.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Red Light Green Light</b></td><td>Move toward the finish on green. Stop when the game switches to red; moving at the wrong time can set you back or eliminate you according to the round.</td></tr></table><h2>Race and completion events</h2><table><tr><th>Event</th><th>How to play</th></tr><tr><td><b>Boat Race</b></td><td>Race the course by boat and finish ahead of the other players.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Horse Race</b></td><td>Race the configured course on horseback. Recovery logic helps return a racer to the course after certain mistakes.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Elytra Race</b></td><td>Fly through the required rings/checkpoint surfaces in order and reach the finish first. Missing the course uses checkpoint/recovery handling rather than letting a shortcut count.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Parkour</b></td><td>Complete the parkour course and checkpoints in order. Falls can return you to the last safe/checkpoint position; finish order determines results.</td></tr></table><h2>BedWars details</h2><p>The event version of BedWars includes resource generators for iron, gold, diamonds and emeralds; item and upgrade shops; Quick Buy; progressive tools; permanent shears; armor tiers; Sharpness, Protection and Haste upgrades; forge upgrades; traps; Heal Pool; Feather Falling; TNT; bed bugs/silverfish; bridge eggs; and bed-controlled respawning.</p><h2>Voting, results and stats</h2><p>Event votes can present up to five choices and show live vote counts. After an event finishes, results can be shown in a trophy-room period before players are returned to the SMP. Event statistics include events played, wins/losses, win ratio, streaks and event-specific records.</p><h2>Related PvP</h2><p>The currently available <a data-page="warzone">Warzone</a> and <a data-page="duels">Death Duels</a> are separate systems and do not depend on Server Events being enabled.</p>`},
"guilds":{title:"Guilds",group:"Gameplay",summary:"Creating and managing guilds, ranks, homes, chat, banks, vaults and relationships.",body:`<p>Guilds are player-created groups with a name, members, ranks, shared homes, chat, a bank/storage system and relationships with other guilds.</p><p>Looking for individual groups and their history? See <a data-special="guilds">Guild pages</a>. This page explains the guild system itself.</p><h2>Opening the guild system</h2><table><tr><td><code>/guild</code> or <code>/g</code></td><td>Open the main guild panel/help for the guild you are in.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild create &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Create a guild. Creation is currently free. Names must be 5–32 characters.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild invite &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Invite another player if your guild rank has permission.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild leave</code></td><td>Leave your current guild.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild kick &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Remove a member if your rank permits it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild promote &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Promote a member through the guild rank structure.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild demote &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Demote a member where permitted.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild disband</code></td><td>Disband the guild if you have the required ownership/management permission. Treat this as destructive.</td></tr></table><div class="fact-grid"><div><b>Maximum members</b><span>20</span></div><div><b>Custom ranks</b><span>up to 10</span></div><div><b>Creation cost</b><span>free</span></div><div><b>Guild bank maximum</b><span>1,000,000</span></div></div><h2>Ranks and permissions</h2><p>Guild ranks decide who can invite or remove players, change guild settings, manage homes, use particular homes, handle shared funds/storage and manage relationships. A member does not automatically receive every guild-management ability just because they are in the guild.</p><h2>Guild homes</h2><table><tr><td><code>/guild sethome [name]</code></td><td>Set a shared guild home. If no name is supplied, the normal default is <code>main</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild homes</code></td><td>List the guild's homes and available home slots.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild home [name]</code></td><td>Teleport to a guild home your rank can use.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild removehome &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Remove a guild home if your rank can manage homes.</td></tr></table><p>Guild-home teleports currently use a 3-second warmup and a 5-second teleport cooldown. Setting a guild home has a 10-minute cooldown. Safety checks can stop or require confirmation for an unsafe location.</p><p>Guild ranks can restrict access to individual homes. Guilds can also configure ally-home access where the relevant relationship and rank permissions allow it.</p><h2>Guild chat</h2><table><tr><td><code>/gc &lt;message&gt;</code></td><td>Send one message directly to guild chat.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/gac &lt;message&gt;</code> / <code>/ga</code></td><td>Send a message to ally chat.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/partychat</code> / <code>/pc</code></td><td>Use party chat where a temporary party is active.</td></tr></table><h2>Bank and vault</h2><p>Guilds have shared financial/storage features controlled by guild-rank permissions. The shared bank has a current maximum balance of 1,000,000 and supports deposit/withdraw controls. The physical guild vault can grow to 54 slots.</p><p>Use the guild menu or guild bank commands shown in game for the exact deposit/withdraw amount syntax available to your rank. Do not assume another member can withdraw simply because they can view the guild balance.</p><h2>Relationships</h2><p>Guilds can maintain ally, enemy, truce and neutral relationships. Other server systems can use those relationships for chat and guild-aware behavior.</p><h2>Java and Bedrock</h2><p>Java players generally use inventory menus while Bedrock players can receive native forms. Both interfaces control the same guild data.</p>`},
"raw-gold":{title:"Raw Gold",group:"Economy",summary:"Physical Raw Gold, bank balances, deposits, withdrawals, payments and the balance leaderboard.",body:`<p>Enthusia's economy is backed by ordinary Minecraft <strong>Raw Gold</strong>. Money can exist as physical items in your inventory or as a persistent bank balance.</p><div class="fact-grid"><div><b>1 Raw Gold</b><span>1 currency</span></div><div><b>1 Raw Gold Block</b><span>9 currency</span></div></div><p>Raw Gold is still a real Minecraft item. Physical currency can be carried, traded, dropped, lost or stolen like other inventory items. Crafting it into Raw Gold Blocks does not remove its value from the economy.</p><h2>Checking your balance</h2><table><tr><td><code>/balance</code></td><td>Show your total wealth, bank balance and physical Raw Gold currently carried.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/bal</code>, <code>/money</code></td><td>Aliases for your balance.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/baltop [page]</code></td><td>Open the balance leaderboard. The ranking cache refreshes roughly every 15 seconds when needed.</td></tr></table><h2>Depositing</h2><table><tr><td><code>/deposit</code></td><td>Deposit all Raw Gold currency items from your inventory.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/deposit all</code></td><td>Same as depositing everything.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/deposit &lt;amount&gt;</code></td><td>Deposit a specific whole-number value when your carried Raw Gold/blocks can represent that amount safely.</td></tr></table><p>A partial deposit does not silently break an unusable denomination into arbitrary change. If the requested amount cannot be represented safely by the physical currency you are carrying, the command can reject it.</p><h2>Withdrawing</h2><p><code>/withdraw &lt;amount&gt;</code> converts bank balance into physical Raw Gold and Raw Gold Blocks. The server checks whether the resulting stacks fit in your inventory before taking the bank funds. If they do not fit, the withdrawal is rejected rather than dropping unexpected currency on the ground.</p><h2>Paying another player</h2><p><code>/pay &lt;player&gt; &lt;amount&gt;</code> sends a positive whole-number amount to another player. You cannot pay yourself.</p><ul><li>Your bank balance is spent first.</li><li>If the bank does not cover the full payment, physical Raw Gold in your inventory can cover the remainder.</li><li>If consuming a physical denomination creates overage, that change is credited back into your bank.</li><li>The recipient receives the payment in their bank balance.</li><li>Offline players can be paid; they receive a notice when they next join.</li></ul><h2>Other systems</h2><p>The same Raw Gold economy is used by features such as the <a data-page="market">Market</a>, duel wagers, rewards and reputation stalking. A system that charges your online balance may be able to use banked and carried currency according to that feature's rules.</p>`},
"homes":{title:"Homes & Teleportation",group:"Gameplay",summary:"TPA requests, personal homes, bed teleports, spawn, warmups and safety checks.",body:`<h2>Standard teleport rules</h2><p>Most normal Enthusia teleports use a <strong>5-second warmup</strong>. Moving more than 0.35 blocks from where the warmup started or taking real damage cancels it. There is currently no extra normal post-teleport cooldown after a successful teleport.</p><p>Teleport commands are blocked during PvP combat. Destinations that require safety checking are searched for a safe position; if one cannot be found, the server fails the teleport instead of forcing you into an invalid block location.</p><h2>Teleport requests</h2><table><tr><th>Command</th><th>Use</th></tr><tr><td><code>/tpa &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Ask to teleport yourself to that player. <code>/tpask</code> is an alias.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpahere &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Ask that player to teleport to you.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpaccept [player]</code></td><td>Accept an incoming request. With no name, accepts the most recent applicable request. <code>/tpyes</code> is an alias.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpadeny [player]</code></td><td>Deny an incoming request. With no name, denies the most recent applicable request. <code>/tpno</code> and <code>/tpdeny</code> are aliases.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpacancel</code></td><td>Cancel your outgoing teleport request(s).</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpignore &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Ignore or unignore teleport requests from a player.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpignore list</code></td><td>Show your saved teleport-ignore list.</td></tr></table><p>Requests expire after 60 seconds. You can have requests involving different players at the same time, but cannot keep sending duplicate pending requests to the same target.</p><p>After a TPA is accepted, the moving player still goes through the normal warmup. The destination follows the other player's live location until the teleport completes rather than permanently locking to where they stood when Accept was clicked.</p><h2>Personal homes</h2><div class="fact-grid"><div><b>Default</b><span>1 home</span></div><div><b>Rank limits</b><span>5 · 10 · 20 homes</span></div></div><table><tr><td><code>/sethome &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Create a named home at your current safe location.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/home</code></td><td>If you have exactly one home, teleport to it. With multiple homes, specify a name.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/home &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Teleport to a specific home.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/homes</code></td><td>Open the homes menu showing names, worlds and coordinates.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/delhome &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Delete one of your homes.</td></tr></table><h3>Homes that became unsafe</h3><p>If blocks around an old home later make it unsafe, the server does not silently put you there. It offers an explicit Teleport Anyway action. That confirmation uses <code>/home &lt;name&gt; force</code>; it bypasses that home's safety warning only.</p><h3>If your home limit decreases</h3><p>If you lose a rank/permission and now own more homes than your new limit, the server does not randomly choose homes to delete. A selection menu lets you choose which homes to keep before the extras are removed.</p><h2>Bed and spawn</h2><table><tr><td><code>/bed</code></td><td>Teleport to your current Minecraft bed-spawn location with normal warmup/safety checks.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/spawn</code></td><td>Teleport to the configured server spawn with the normal warmup.</td></tr></table><p>Normal deaths currently respawn at server spawn even if you have slept in a bed. The bed location remains useful for <code>/bed</code>.</p><h2>First join</h2><p>A brand-new player starts at spawn, receives an initial bed-spawn at spawn and gets 8 Cooked Beef plus a Stone Sword, Stone Axe, Stone Shovel and Stone Pickaxe.</p>`},
"warzone":{title:"Warzone",group:"PvP",summary:"Current Warzone kits, weekly rotation, random modifiers, restrictions and player commands.",body:`<p>The Warzone uses a rotating set of combat rules. Spawn and the Market are excluded from the effective Warzone modifier area even where those regions overlap the larger PvP area.</p><h2>Check the rules before fighting</h2><table><tr><td><code>/warzone</code></td><td>Open the Warzone menu.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone info</code></td><td>Show the active selection, modifiers, any current override and next automatic transition.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone modifiers</code></td><td>Show the modifiers active right now.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone modifier list</code></td><td>List the configured modifiers and their descriptions.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone kit</code></td><td>Show whether the current selection is a named kit.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone kits</code></td><td>Browse the configured kits.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone items</code></td><td>Show the current item/ability restrictions.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone next</code></td><td>Show the next automatic Warzone selection/change.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone schedule</code></td><td>Show the current rotation schedule.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone menu</code></td><td>Open the Warzone GUI.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone help</code></td><td>Show Warzone command help.</td></tr></table><h2>Weekly rotation</h2><p>The automatic selection changes once per week at <strong>12:00 PM America/Indiana/Indianapolis</strong> and repeats a four-week cycle:</p><ol><li><b>SMP kit</b></li><li><b>Random modifiers</b></li><li><b>Vanilla kit</b></li><li><b>Random modifiers</b></li></ol><p>Warnings are sent 1 hour, 30 minutes, 10 minutes, 5 minutes and 1 minute before a scheduled change.</p><h2>Fixed kits</h2><table><tr><th>Kit</th><th>Rules</th></tr><tr><td><b>SMP</b></td><td>Temporary cobwebs; 5s Wind Charge cooldown; 5s Ender Pearl cooldown; 5s Spear Lunge cooldown; Maces disabled.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Mace Nerf</b></td><td>Successful Mace attacks receive a 10s cooldown; Spear Lunge receives a 5s cooldown.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Spear</b></td><td>Successful Spear damage receives a 10s cooldown; Spear Lunge receives a 10s cooldown.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Vanilla</b></td><td>No rotating Warzone modifier is applied; normal vanilla/server combat rules remain.</td></tr></table><h2>Random weeks</h2><p>A random week selects 1–3 compatible modifiers. The number-of-modifiers weighting is 35% for one, 45% for two and 20% for three. The same exact random set cannot immediately repeat, and conflicting rules are not selected together.</p><table><tr><th>Modifier</th><th>Effect</th><th>Weight</th></tr><tr><td>Cobwebs</td><td>Temporary Warzone cobweb placement</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>No Lunge</td><td>Disable Spear Lunge but not ordinary spear use</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>5s Lunge</td><td>5-second cooldown after a successful Lunge</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>10s Lunge</td><td>10-second cooldown after a successful Lunge</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>No Spears</td><td>Disable spear launches and spear damage</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>5s Spear Damage</td><td>5-second cooldown after successful spear damage</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>10s Spear Damage</td><td>10-second cooldown after successful spear damage</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>No Maces</td><td>Disable Mace use</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Mace Cooldown</td><td>10-second cooldown after a successful Mace attack</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>No Ender Pearls</td><td>Disable Ender Pearls</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>5s Pearl</td><td>5-second cooldown after a successful throw</td><td>9</td></tr><tr><td>10s Pearl</td><td>10-second cooldown after a successful throw</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>No Wind Charges</td><td>Disable Wind Charges</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>5s Wind Charge</td><td>5-second cooldown after a successful use</td><td>9</td></tr><tr><td>10s Wind Charge</td><td>10-second cooldown after a successful use</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>Elytra, No Rockets</td><td>Allow gliding under the applicable rule but block actual firework propulsion</td><td>1</td></tr></table><h2>How cooldowns start</h2><p>Cooldowns begin from the relevant successful action rather than every attempted click. A Pearl cooldown begins after a successful throw; a Mace cooldown after a successful attack; a Spear-damage cooldown after accepted positive damage; and a Lunge cooldown after the Lunge movement is actually accepted. Misses and cancelled actions do not create fake cooldowns.</p><h2>Temporary cobwebs</h2><p>When the Cobweb modifier is active, managed Warzone cobwebs last 60 seconds. They are also cleared when the active Warzone rule set changes so old event cobwebs do not become permanent map clutter.</p><h2>Leaving while combat-tagged</h2><p>Some spear restrictions can follow a combat-tagged player briefly after crossing out of the Warzone so stepping over the boundary does not instantly remove those rules. Current carryover applies to the 5s/10s Spear Lunge modes, No Spears and the 5s/10s Spear-damage modes. Cobweb, Mace, Pearl, Wind Charge and Elytra modifiers do not currently carry outside in the same way.</p><h2>Elytra during combat</h2><p>A combat-tagged player cannot normally begin gliding under the Warzone combat policy. A player already gliding when tagged is not forcibly knocked down. When the Elytra/No Rockets rule applies, gliding can be allowed while firework boosting itself is blocked.</p><h2>End island restriction</h2><div class="callout"><b>Separate from the weekly rotation:</b> Maces and Spears are blocked within 1,024 blocks of the center of the main End island.</div>`},
"duels":{title:"Death Duels",group:"PvP",summary:"How to challenge players, configure fight rules, wager Raw Gold and claim victor's spoils.",body:`<p>Death Duels are consensual 1v1 fights in Enthusia's dedicated duel arena. They are <strong>not keep-inventory duels</strong>: the gear and experience you bring can be put at real risk.</p><h2>Starting a duel</h2><p><code>/duel &lt;player&gt;</code> opens the duel builder against that player. A request lasts 120 seconds.</p><p>Before a duel can start, both players must be online, free of another duel flow and combat tag, inside the matchmaking area, able to afford the wager, and not holding unclaimed victor's spoils. Same-IP duels are currently blocked.</p><table><tr><td><code>/duel review</code></td><td>Open the incoming challenge and review every selected rule.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel accept</code></td><td>Accept the reviewed challenge.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel deny</code></td><td>Deny the incoming challenge.</td></tr></table><h2>Building rules</h2><table><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td><b>No Building or Breaking</b></td><td>No block placement or breaking during the duel.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Limited — Utilities Only</b></td><td>Original arena terrain stays protected; Cobwebs, Water Buckets, buttons and pressure plates can be used.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Limited — All Placeable Blocks</b></td><td>Normal placement is allowed and duel-placed blocks can be broken, while original terrain remains protected.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Place & Break</b></td><td>Full placement and original-terrain breaking, but only on a map that explicitly supports it. The default Flat Arena does not.</td></tr></table><h2>Explosives and combat items</h2><p>Where the chosen building/map rules support them, the challenge can separately allow End Crystals/Respawn Anchors, TNT Minecarts, and TNT/other explosive blocks.</p><p>The challenger can independently allow or block Ender Pearls, Wind Charges, Maces, Chorus Fruit, Spears, Elytras and Ender Chests. Pearl and Wind Charge cooldown choices cycle through 0s, 5s, 10s, 15s and 30s.</p><h2>Wagers</h2><p>Each player can wager up to <strong>100,000</strong>. The builder amount is per player, so a 500 wager means each player stakes 500 and the winner receives the 1,000 combined pot. Both stakes are taken before the fight. A valid draw/refund path returns each player's stake.</p><h2>Fight start and arena rules</h2><p>Before release, both players are normalized for the fight: health, hunger and saturation are restored; fire/freeze/arrows/fall distance and potion effects are cleared; Survival mode is enforced; and the current start countdown is 5 seconds.</p><p>During the fight, participant chat is disabled, almost all commands are blocked, participants cannot teleport out or leave the arena, and outside players cannot interfere.</p><table><tr><td><code>/duel info</code> / <code>/duel settings</code></td><td>Review the active duel rules.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel draw</code></td><td>Request a mutual draw.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/draw</code></td><td>Shortcut for the same mutual draw request.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/surrender</code> / <code>/duel surrender</code></td><td>Despite the name, currently also requests a mutual draw; it does not instantly concede.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel cancel</code></td><td>Cancel a queued duel before it starts; during an active fight it routes through the draw/cancel flow.</td></tr></table><h2>Death and victor's spoils</h2><p>The loser's item drops are captured into a durable vault for the winner rather than scattered across the arena floor.</p><table><tr><td><code>/vault</code></td><td>Open your victor's-spoils vault.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel vault</code>, <code>/duelvault</code>, <code>/spoils</code>, <code>/claimspoils</code></td><td>Aliases/paths to the same spoils system.</td></tr></table><p>Items that do not fit stay in the vault rather than being deleted. Unclaimed spoils expire after 24 hours, and a player with unclaimed spoils cannot start or accept another duel until they handle them.</p><p>A normal duel loss does not restore the loser's pre-duel inventory. Current death handling also clears the loser's dropped XP rather than transferring that experience to the winner.</p><h2>Disconnecting</h2><p>A disconnected participant has a 30-second reconnect grace period. Rejoining in time returns them to their arena position and the duel continues. Staying offline past the deadline forfeits: the opponent wins and the disconnecting player's at-risk loadout is handled as the loss rather than being protected by logging out.</p><h2>Stats</h2><table><tr><td><code>/stats</code></td><td>Open your duel statistics where the command permission is available.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/stats &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>View another profile where your permission allows it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel stats</code></td><td>Duel-subcommand path to stats.</td></tr></table><p>Stats include matches, wins, losses, draws, current/best win streak, disconnect-forfeit losses and win/loss ratio.</p><h2>Spectating</h2><p>The duel system has controlled watch mode through <code>/duel watch</code>, <code>/duel spectate</code> or <code>/duel stands</code>, and <code>/duel leave</code>/<code>/duel unwatch</code> to exit. Spectating is permission-controlled, so it should only be expected when your current rank grants access.</p>`},
"playtime":{title:"Playtime",group:"Progression",summary:"Total, active and AFK time, leaderboards, first joins and active-playtime numeral tiers.",body:`<p>Enthusia tracks <strong>total</strong>, <strong>active</strong> and <strong>AFK/non-active</strong> playtime separately.</p><div class="fact-grid"><div><b>Idle</b><span>after 60 seconds without recognized activity</span></div><div><b>AFK</b><span>after 5 minutes without recognized activity</span></div></div><p>Movement, interactions, combat actions, block actions, chat and commands can count as activity. Idle and AFK minutes go into the non-active bucket instead of advancing active-playtime progression.</p><h2>Your playtime</h2><table><tr><td><code>/playtime</code> / <code>/pt</code></td><td>Open your playtime GUI with lifetime total, active and AFK time.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/playtime &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>View another player's ordinary playtime where your permission allows it.</td></tr></table><h2>Leaderboards</h2><p><code>/playtime top [active|afk|total] [today|7d|30d|all] [page]</code> opens the leaderboard directly with optional filters.</p><p>You can compare total, active or AFK time for today, the last 7 days, last 30 days or all time. The GUI includes player heads/ranks, all three time totals, your own position and page controls.</p><h2>Automation-resistant active time</h2><p>The activity tracker looks for unusually regular clicking, repeated rotations, movement loops and repeating action sequences. This is not an anti-cheat punishment: it only decides whether repetitive behavior keeps earning active-playtime credit.</p><p>The first 10 consecutive suspicious minutes can still count as active. After that, continuous suspicious activity stops adding active time until sufficiently varied legitimate activity clears the state.</p><h2>Numeral progression</h2><p><code>/playtime numerals</code>, <code>/roman</code>, <code>/numerals</code> and <code>/rn</code> show the numeral progression. Numerals use <strong>active</strong> playtime, not total connection time.</p><table><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Active hours</th></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>II</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>III</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>IV</td><td>45</td></tr><tr><td>V</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>VI</td><td>170</td></tr><tr><td>VII</td><td>320</td></tr><tr><td>VIII</td><td>580</td></tr><tr><td>IX</td><td>1,090</td></tr><tr><td>X</td><td>2,000</td></tr><tr><td>Y</td><td>5,000</td></tr><tr><td>Z</td><td>15,000</td></tr></table><h2>First joins and last seen</h2><table><tr><td><code>/firstjoin</code> / <code>/fj</code></td><td>Show your recorded first-join date/time and how long ago it was.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/firstjoin &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Look up another player's first-join record where available.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/seen &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Show whether a player is online or their last-seen time where your current rank has the required permission.</td></tr></table>`},
"reputation":{title:"Reputation",group:"Progression",summary:"Giving reviews, reputation categories, score effects, leaderboards and stalking low-reputation players.",body:`<p>Reputation records player-to-player reviews rather than being only a like/dislike total. Each entry has a category and can include a written reason up to 256 characters.</p><div class="fact-grid"><div><b>Positive review</b><span>+1</span></div><div><b>Negative review</b><span>-2</span></div><div><b>Edit/change cooldown</b><span>24 hours per giver/target entry</span></div><div><b>Stalkable</b><span>-12 reputation or lower</span></div></div><h2>Commands</h2><table><tr><td><code>/rep</code> / <code>/reputation</code></td><td>Open your reputation profile.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Open another player's profile and review history.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep top</code></td><td>Open the top reputation leaderboard.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep bottom</code></td><td>Open the lowest reputation leaderboard.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep reviews [player]</code></td><td>Show a compact recent-review view.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep give &lt;player&gt; &lt;category&gt; &lt;reason&gt;</code></td><td>Direct-command alternative to giving reputation through the profile GUI.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep stalk &lt;player&gt; [days]</code></td><td>Purchase a stalking subscription for a player at -12 or lower.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep stalk list</code></td><td>View your active stalking subscriptions and remaining time.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep stalk cancel &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Cancel one of your subscriptions.</td></tr></table><h2>Categories</h2><table><tr><th>Positive (+1)</th><th>Negative (-2)</th></tr><tr><td>Was Kind</td><td>Scammed</td></tr><tr><td>Helped Me</td><td>Spawn Killed</td></tr><tr><td>Gave Items/Money</td><td>Griefed</td></tr><tr><td>Trustworthy</td><td>Trapped</td></tr><tr><td>Good Stall</td><td>Scam Stall</td></tr></table><h2>Gameplay effects</h2><table><tr><th>Score</th><th>Configured effect</th></tr><tr><td>+5</td><td>+1% movement speed</td></tr><tr><td>+10</td><td>+3% movement speed; +5% potion duration</td></tr><tr><td>+15</td><td>+5% movement speed; +10% potion duration</td></tr><tr><td>-5</td><td>-1% movement speed</td></tr><tr><td>-6</td><td>3s Ender Pearl cooldown; -5% Elytra-rocket duration</td></tr><tr><td>-7</td><td>-3% movement; 2s Wind Charge cooldown; -10% rocket duration</td></tr><tr><td>-10</td><td>-5% movement; 5s Ender Pearl cooldown; glowing</td></tr><tr><td>-12</td><td>Stalkable; -10% potion duration</td></tr><tr><td>-15</td><td>7s Pearl; 5s Wind Charge; -15% rocket duration</td></tr><tr><td>-20</td><td>10s Pearl; 10s Wind Charge; -10% movement; -15% potion duration; -25% rocket duration; red glow</td></tr></table><p>Movement, glow and potion-duration effects are region-aware and apply in the configured spawn/Warzone effect areas. Pearl and Wind Charge penalties apply specifically in the Warzone. Death Duel participants are generally exempt so reputation does not distort a configured duel ruleset.</p><h2>Stalking</h2><p>A player at -12 reputation or lower can be subscribed to for <strong>100 Raw Gold per day</strong>, from 1 to 7 days. Stalking is not a live GPS or compass.</p><p>While the subscriber is online, a genuine same-world transition by the target from Market, Spawn or Wilderness into the Warzone sends an alert with the exact block coordinates where that target entered the Warzone.</p>`},
"tags":{title:"Tags, Rewards & Cosmetics",group:"Progression",summary:"Tags, achievements, daily Raw Gold, cosmetic unlocks and reward progression.",body:`<h2>Tags</h2><p><code>/tags</code> opens Your Tags. It contains the tags you have actually unlocked or been granted.</p><ul><li>Click an owned tag to equip it.</li><li>Only one tag can be selected at a time.</li><li>Use Clear Tag in the menu to remove the selected tag.</li><li>If you own no tags, the menu shows that rather than pretending locked tags are usable.</li></ul><h2>Achievements and rewards</h2><p><code>/rewards</code> opens the progression catalog. It is divided into Playtime, Mining, Combat, Deaths, Economy and Misc categories and contains roughly 100 configured rewards.</p><p>Rewards can grant tags, Raw Gold, normal Minecraft items, Lore Items and permission-based feature/cosmetic unlocks.</p><table><tr><th>Example</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Reward</th></tr><tr><td>Trail Starter</td><td>Walk 20,000 blocks</td><td>Trail cosmetic</td></tr><tr><td>First Blood FX</td><td>10 player kills</td><td>Kill effect</td></tr><tr><td>Arrow Flair</td><td>50 projectile hits</td><td>Projectile cosmetic</td></tr><tr><td>GG Messages</td><td>5 player kills</td><td>Kill-message cosmetic</td></tr><tr><td>Block Game Addict</td><td>24 active-playtime hours</td><td>Tag + 500 Raw Gold</td></tr><tr><td>Payday</td><td>5 total-playtime hours</td><td>150 Raw Gold</td></tr><tr><td>Starter Pack</td><td>Mine 250 stone</td><td>2 Golden Apples</td></tr><tr><td>High Roller</td><td>Hold 100,000 currency</td><td>Tag + 500 Raw Gold</td></tr><tr><td>Market Access</td><td>10 total-playtime hours</td><td>Market-stall access</td></tr><tr><td>Reputation Unlocked</td><td>5 active-playtime hours</td><td>Reputation access</td></tr></table><h3>Anti-farming</h3><p>Kill-based achievement progress only counts up to five qualifying kills for the same killer/victim pair in a rolling 60-minute window. This limits progression farming; it is not an automatic punishment.</p><p>Natural-resource mining rewards also track natural blocks so repeatedly placing and re-mining the same tracked ore/block does not create unlimited progression.</p><h2>Daily rewards</h2><p><code>/daily</code> opens the daily reward menu. Missing a calendar day resets the next successful claim to Day 1. After Day 7 the streak can keep growing, while the payout remains 50 per day.</p><table><tr><th>Day</th><th>Raw Gold</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>30</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>40</td></tr><tr><td>7+</td><td>50/day</td></tr></table><p>The daily date boundary uses America/Indiana/Indianapolis time. The current daily system also has a shared-IP fairness limit, with household exceptions handled by staff when appropriate.</p><h2>Cosmetics</h2><p><code>/cosmetics</code> opens the cosmetic menu. Categories are Projectiles, Kill Messages, Kill Effects, Death Effects, Trails, Join Messages, Quit Messages and Misc.</p><p>You can have one selected cosmetic per category. Clicking an unlocked cosmetic selects it; clicking the already-active cosmetic again disables that category selection. Locked cosmetics can remain visible so you can see what exists and what still needs to be unlocked.</p><ul><li><b>Projectile cosmetics</b> add effects to launched projectiles.</li><li><b>Kill effects</b> play at a defeated player's location.</li><li><b>Death effects</b> play when the owner dies.</li><li><b>Trails</b> follow the player while moving/active.</li><li><b>Kill messages</b> replace that player's normal PvP death-message style.</li><li><b>Join/Quit messages</b> replace the owner's normal join or leave message.</li></ul>`},
"autoclicker":{title:"AutoClicker",group:"Gameplay",summary:"How to use Enthusia's server-side stationary hostile-mob farming AutoClicker.",body:`<p><code>/autoclick</code> is a server-side automatic melee helper intended for stationary hostile-mob farms. It works for both Java and Bedrock; no client mod is required.</p><h2>Commands</h2><table><tr><td><code>/autoclick</code></td><td>Toggle cooldown mode. The server attempts an attack whenever your normal attack cooldown is fully ready.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/autoclick &lt;ticks&gt;</code></td><td>Start fixed-interval mode with that many Minecraft ticks between attempts.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/autoclick off</code></td><td>Stop the session. <code>stop</code> and <code>disable</code> are equivalent.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/autoclick status</code></td><td>Show whether AutoClicker is off, using cooldown mode or using a fixed interval.</td></tr></table><h2>Fixed interval examples</h2><table><tr><th>Command</th><th>Attempt interval</th></tr><tr><td><code>/autoclick 1</code></td><td>Every tick — up to 20 attempts per second</td></tr><tr><td><code>/autoclick 5</code></td><td>Every 0.25 seconds</td></tr><tr><td><code>/autoclick 10</code></td><td>Every 0.5 seconds</td></tr><tr><td><code>/autoclick 20</code></td><td>Every 1 second</td></tr></table><p>The minimum current fixed interval is one tick. A fast attempt rate does not bypass Minecraft attack strength: actual attacks still use the normal server attack path and cooldown-scaled damage.</p><h2>Targets</h2><ul><li>3-block attack range.</li><li>Players are never deliberately targeted.</li><li>Armor stands, villagers, wandering traders, tamed animals and normal passive/water/ambient mobs are excluded.</li><li>Valid hostile living mobs under your crosshair can be attacked.</li><li>A small 0.35-block target ray makes aiming slightly forgiving without turning it into an area attack.</li></ul><h2>When it stops</h2><p>Your activation location becomes the session anchor. Moving more than <strong>0.75 blocks</strong> away stops AutoClicker.</p><p>It also stops when you enter PvP combat, open a non-default inventory/menu/trade, teleport, change worlds, die, disconnect or switch into a game mode where automated attacks are not allowed. A stopped session has to be enabled again manually.</p><h2>Walls and farm windows</h2><p>Attacks cannot pass through blocking collision shapes. Full walls stop targeting; passable blocks can be ignored; partial blocks such as slabs or trapdoors use their real collision shape. This allows normal mob-farm windows without simply hitting through walls.</p>`},
"base-privacy":{title:"Base Privacy",group:"Gameplay",summary:"How Enthusia hides selected base clues and how to build around the privacy system.",body:`<p>Enthusia reduces selected entity and block-entity clues that can otherwise reveal hidden bases through client-side debugging, pie-chart or ESP-style information. The real entities/blocks continue to exist normally on the server.</p><h2>Distance and visibility</h2><div class="fact-grid"><div><b>Within ~24 blocks</b><span>Managed clues are always shown.</span></div><div><b>~24–48 blocks</b><span>Real line-of-sight/occlusion is checked.</span></div><div><b>Beyond ~48 blocks</b><span>Managed clues remain hidden until eligible to show.</span></div><div><b>Occlusion target</b><span>3 blocking samples along the ray.</span></div></div><p>In practice, a clue buried behind several solid blocks is better protected than the same clue placed directly against an exposed outer wall.</p><h2>Entity clues covered</h2><p>Managed entity types include villagers, copper golems, armadillos, wolves, cats, ocelots, allays, bees, iron golems, snow golems, item/glow item frames, armor stands and paintings.</p><h2>Block-entity clues covered</h2><p>Managed block entities include campfires and soul campfires, decorated pots, bells, jukeboxes, conduits, beacons, moving pistons, shulker boxes, signs and hanging signs, banners, beds, heads and skulls.</p><h2>What it does not protect</h2><ul><li>Players are not hidden from one another.</li><li>Ordinary blocks are not turned invisible and this is not an ore X-ray hider.</li><li>It does not stop normal exploration.</li><li>It does not hide exposed builds, roads, player trails, maps or coordinates someone shares.</li><li>It does not make a base invisible at close range.</li></ul><h2>Practical base-hiding advice</h2><p>Keep revealing entities and block entities inside terrain or behind multiple solid blocks rather than at the outside surface. Treat the system as protection against unusual client-information leakage, not as a replacement for choosing a hidden location and controlling who knows your coordinates.</p>`},
"voting":{title:"Voting",group:"Progression",summary:"Vote rewards, daily vote-site completion, streak mining boosts and Vote Party.",body:`<p>Voting supports the server and pays Raw Gold while building a daily streak.</p><table><tr><td><code>/vote</code></td><td>Open/show the server voting options.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/votesites</code></td><td>Show the individual vote sites.</td></tr></table><h2>Normal rewards</h2><p>Each accepted vote pays <strong>1–10 Raw Gold</strong>. Completing all five vote sites in one day gives an additional <strong>20 Raw Gold</strong>.</p><h2>Streak mining boost</h2><p>At a 3+ day streak, a vote can activate a 20-minute gold-mining multiplier:</p><table><tr><th>Streak</th><th>Boost</th></tr><tr><td>3–6 days</td><td>1.5×</td></tr><tr><td>7–29 days</td><td>2×</td></tr><tr><td>30+ days</td><td>3×</td></tr></table><h2>Vote Party</h2><p>Every 100 server votes starts a 30-minute Vote Party with a <strong>2× gold-mining multiplier</strong>. Vote Party multiplies with an active personal streak boost, so the two systems can stack.</p>`},
"trivia":{title:"Trivia",group:"Community",summary:"Automatic chat trivia, answer timing, points, Raw Gold rewards and leaderboards.",body:`<p>Trivia questions run automatically about every 15 minutes. Players normally have 30 seconds to answer the current question.</p><table><tr><th>Difficulty</th><th>Raw Gold</th><th>Points</th></tr><tr><td>Easy</td><td>5</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Medium</td><td>10</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Hard</td><td>15</td><td>3</td></tr></table><h2>Commands</h2><table><tr><td><code>/trivia stats</code></td><td>Show your trivia statistics.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/trivia top</code></td><td>Show the trivia leaderboard.</td></tr></table><p>Questions include multiple-choice and true/false formats. The point total is separate from the Raw Gold payout, allowing a long-term trivia leaderboard rather than ranking only by money earned.</p>`},
"giveaways":{title:"Giveaways",group:"Community",summary:"Entering server giveaways and receiving giveaway results.",body:`<p>When a server giveaway is active, <code>/giveaway</code> opens its menu. Entry is free.</p><p>New giveaways are announced server-wide. The menu shows the active giveaway information and lets eligible players enter; the winner is announced when the giveaway closes.</p>`},
"chat":{title:"Chat & Messages",group:"Server",summary:"Private messages, reply behavior, channels, ignores, colors, emojis and chat controls.",body:`<h2>Private messages</h2><table><tr><td><code>/msg &lt;player&gt; &lt;message&gt;</code></td><td>Send a private message.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tell</code>, <code>/w</code>, <code>/whisper</code></td><td>Aliases for private messaging.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/r &lt;message&gt;</code></td><td>Reply to the most recent private-message conversation — either the player you last messaged or the player who most recently messaged you.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/reply &lt;message&gt;</code></td><td>Alias for <code>/r</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/msgtoggle</code></td><td>Toggle whether you receive normal private messages, where your permissions/settings allow it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/ignore &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Ignore/unignore a player's chat/message interaction.</td></tr></table><h2>Channels</h2><table><tr><td><code>/c</code> / <code>/channel</code></td><td>Open or change chat-channel controls.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/gc &lt;message&gt;</code></td><td>Send a one-off guild-chat message.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/gac &lt;message&gt;</code> / <code>/ga</code></td><td>Send a one-off ally-chat message.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/partychat</code> / <code>/pc</code></td><td>Use party chat when a party is active.</td></tr></table><h2>Appearance and convenience</h2><table><tr><td><code>/chatcolor</code></td><td>Open or configure chat-color choices available to your rank.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/colorcodes</code></td><td>Show supported chat color/format codes.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/emoji</code> / <code>/emojis</code></td><td>Open/list the chat emoji feature.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/togglesound</code></td><td>Toggle supported chat/message sounds.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/ping</code></td><td>Show ping information.</td></tr></table>`},
"market":{title:"Market",group:"Economy",summary:"Player stalls, sign shops, rent, auctions, search tools and guild-aware market ownership.",body:`<p>The Market is Enthusia's protected player-trading area. Players can own stalls, create container-backed shops, pay rent and bid on timed stall auctions.</p><div class="fact-grid"><div><b>Default owned stalls</b><span>1</span></div><div><b>Shop tax</b><span>2%</span></div><div><b>Rent</b><span>100/day</span></div><div><b>Grace period</b><span>3 days</span></div></div><h2>Main commands</h2><table><tr><td><code>/em</code> / <code>/enthusiamarket</code></td><td>Open/use the main Enthusia Market command system.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/em auctions</code> / <code>/auctions</code></td><td>Browse stall auctions.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/em bid &lt;auctionId&gt; &lt;amount&gt;</code></td><td>Bid on a stall auction.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/em stall info &lt;stallId&gt;</code></td><td>Inspect a stall and its current information.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/shop search &lt;item&gt;</code> / <code>/shopsearch</code></td><td>Search market shops for an item.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/shopvault</code></td><td>Open the shop-related vault where the market provides stored proceeds/items.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guildshop</code></td><td>Access guild-aware shop functionality where applicable.</td></tr></table><h2>Stalls</h2><p>A stall is a protected build/trading space in the Market. Available stalls can be purchased through their market flow or acquired in an auction. Owners can manage members and the stall's shop space.</p><p>The default player limit is one owned stall, with a one-owned-stall-per-IP fairness rule in the current setup.</p><h2>Shops</h2><table><tr><th>Type</th><th>Use</th></tr><tr><td>SELL</td><td>You stock items; buyers pay you.</td></tr><tr><td>BUY</td><td>Other players sell the requested items to your shop.</td></tr><tr><td>TRADE</td><td>Item-for-item barter rather than a normal currency sale.</td></tr></table><p>Shops are tied to containers inside stalls. The current transaction tax is 2%.</p><h2>Rent</h2><p>Rent is currently 100 per day. If the stall cannot pay, it enters a 3-day grace period and its shops freeze. Paying during grace returns the stall to normal. If grace expires, the stall can move into an emergency auction.</p><h2>Auctions</h2><div class="fact-grid"><div><b>Minimum duration</b><span>15 minutes</span></div><div><b>Default duration</b><span>24 hours</span></div><div><b>Maximum duration</b><span>7 days</span></div><div><b>Minimum starting bid</b><span>100</span></div></div><p>A bid placed in the final 30 seconds extends the auction by 30 seconds to reduce last-second sniping. The current auction fee is 0%.</p><h2>Java and Bedrock</h2><p>Java uses inventory-style interfaces where appropriate; Bedrock players can receive Bedrock-friendly forms for the same market state.</p>`},
"commands":{title:"Commands",group:"Reference",summary:"A detailed reference for Enthusia player commands, useful aliases, subcommands and currently unavailable roots.",body:`<p>Commands are grouped by what they do. Aliases are shown with the main command so you do not have to search several entries for the same feature.</p><h2>Server information and links</h2><table><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td><code>/rules</code></td><td>Show/open the server rules.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/website</code></td><td>Get the official Enthusia website.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/store</code></td><td>Get the official Enthusia store.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/discord</code></td><td>Get the official Discord.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/newbie</code></td><td>Open/show new-player information.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/info</code></td><td>Show server information where provided by the current server setup.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/position</code> / <code>/pos</code></td><td>Show your current position/coordinates.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/nextrestart</code> / <code>/restartschedule</code></td><td>Show the next scheduled server restart/restart schedule.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/ping</code></td><td>Show ping information.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/firstjoin [player]</code></td><td>Show first-join time. Aliases: <code>/fj</code>, <code>/firstjoined</code>, <code>/fjoined</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/seen &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Show online/last-seen information where your rank currently has permission.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/report</code></td><td>Open/use the server's player-report flow where available.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/hub</code></td><td>Leave the SMP for the network hub where the proxy command is available.</td></tr></table><h2>Teleportation and homes</h2><table><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td><code>/tpa &lt;player&gt;</code> / <code>/tpask</code></td><td>Request to teleport yourself to another player.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpahere &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Request that another player teleport to you.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpaccept [player]</code> / <code>/tpyes</code> / <code>/accept</code></td><td>Accept a request; without a name, use the most recent applicable request.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpadeny [player]</code> / <code>/tpno</code> / <code>/tpdeny</code> / <code>/deny</code></td><td>Deny an incoming request.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpacancel</code></td><td>Cancel outgoing TPA request(s).</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpignore &lt;player&gt;</code> / <code>/tpaignore</code></td><td>Ignore/unignore teleport requests from a player.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tpignore list</code></td><td>View your TPA ignore list.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/sethome &lt;name&gt;</code> / <code>/homeset</code></td><td>Set a personal home.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/home [name]</code></td><td>Teleport to a home.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/homes</code></td><td>Open/list your homes.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/delhome &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Delete a home.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/home &lt;name&gt; force</code></td><td>Use the explicit unsafe-home confirmation path after the server warns you.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/bed</code></td><td>Teleport to your Minecraft bed-spawn location.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/spawn</code></td><td>Teleport to server spawn.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tptoggle</code></td><td>Toggle supported incoming teleport behavior where the active permission/config provides it.</td></tr></table><h2>Raw Gold and economy</h2><table><tr><td><code>/balance</code> / <code>/bal</code></td><td>Show total, banked and carried Raw Gold.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/deposit [all|amount]</code></td><td>Move physical Raw Gold into your bank.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/withdraw &lt;amount&gt;</code> / <code>/withdrawl</code></td><td>Convert bank balance into physical Raw Gold.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/pay &lt;player&gt; &lt;amount&gt;</code></td><td>Pay another player; bank money is used first, then carried currency if needed.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/baltop [page]</code> / <code>/balancetop</code></td><td>Open the balance leaderboard.</td></tr></table><h2>Market</h2><table><tr><td><code>/em</code> / <code>/enthusiamarket</code></td><td>Main Market command/menu.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/em stall info &lt;stallId&gt;</code></td><td>Inspect a stall.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/em auctions</code> / <code>/auctions</code></td><td>Browse stall auctions.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/em bid &lt;auctionId&gt; &lt;amount&gt;</code></td><td>Bid on an auction.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/shop</code></td><td>Use the market shop command system.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/shop search &lt;item&gt;</code> / <code>/shopsearch</code></td><td>Search shops for an item.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/finditem</code></td><td>Item-finding/search command exposed by the current server; use its in-game syntax/help for the exact search arguments.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/shopvault</code></td><td>Open the market/shop vault where available.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guildshop</code></td><td>Open guild-aware shop functionality where available.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/arm</code></td><td>Legacy/compatibility market-region command root; use <code>/em</code> for the current Market system.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/itemshops</code> / <code>/itemshopstutorial</code></td><td>Legacy ItemShops roots retained by the command allowlist. The current player market is EnthusiaMarket.</td></tr></table><h2>Guilds and group chat</h2><table><tr><td><code>/guild</code> / <code>/g</code></td><td>Open/use the guild system.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild create &lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Create a guild.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild invite &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Invite a player if your rank permits it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild kick &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Remove a member if permitted.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild promote &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Promote a member.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild demote &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Demote a member.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild leave</code></td><td>Leave your guild.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild sethome [name]</code></td><td>Set a guild home.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild home [name]</code></td><td>Teleport to a permitted guild home.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/guild homes</code></td><td>List guild homes.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/gc &lt;message&gt;</code></td><td>Guild chat.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/gac &lt;message&gt;</code> / <code>/ga</code></td><td>Ally chat.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/partychat</code> / <code>/pc</code></td><td>Party chat where a party is active.</td></tr></table><h2>Private messages and chat</h2><table><tr><td><code>/msg &lt;player&gt; &lt;message&gt;</code></td><td>Private message.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tell</code> / <code>/w</code> / <code>/whisper</code></td><td>Private-message aliases.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/r &lt;message&gt;</code> / <code>/reply</code></td><td>Reply to the player you last messaged or who most recently messaged you.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/msgtoggle</code></td><td>Toggle supported private-message receiving.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/ignore &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Ignore/unignore another player's supported chat/message interaction.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/c</code> / <code>/channel</code></td><td>Chat channel controls.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/chatcolor</code></td><td>Choose chat-color options your rank has unlocked.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/colorcodes</code></td><td>Show supported color/format codes.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/emoji</code> / <code>/emojis</code></td><td>Emoji list/menu.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/togglesound</code></td><td>Toggle supported chat/message sounds.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/interactivechat</code></td><td>Interactive-chat command root; detailed options depend on the current chat integration.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/group</code></td><td>Chat-group command root where your rank has access.</td></tr></table><h2>Playtime and progression</h2><table><tr><td><code>/playtime</code> / <code>/pt</code></td><td>Open your total/active/AFK playtime.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/playtime top [active|afk|total] [today|7d|30d|all] [page]</code></td><td>Open a filtered playtime leaderboard.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/playtime numerals</code> / <code>/roman</code> / <code>/numerals</code> / <code>/rn</code></td><td>Show active-playtime numeral progression.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/firstjoin [player]</code> / <code>/fj</code></td><td>First-join record.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tags</code></td><td>View/equip your unlocked tags.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rewards</code></td><td>Browse achievements and rewards.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/cosmetics</code></td><td>Choose unlocked cosmetics.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/daily</code></td><td>View/claim the daily Raw Gold reward.</td></tr></table><h2>Reputation</h2><table><tr><td><code>/rep</code> / <code>/reputation</code></td><td>Open your reputation profile.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Open another profile.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep top</code> / <code>/rep bottom</code></td><td>Open reputation leaderboards.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep reviews [player]</code></td><td>Recent review list.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep give &lt;player&gt; &lt;category&gt; &lt;reason&gt;</code></td><td>Give reputation directly.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep stalk &lt;player&gt; [days]</code></td><td>Buy a stalking subscription for a target at -12 or below.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep stalk list</code></td><td>List active subscriptions.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/rep stalk cancel &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Cancel a subscription.</td></tr></table><h2>Warzone</h2><table><tr><td><code>/warzone</code> / <code>/warzone menu</code></td><td>Open the Warzone menu.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone info</code></td><td>Detailed current status.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone modifiers</code></td><td>Current modifiers.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone modifier list</code></td><td>All configured modifiers/descriptions.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone kit</code> / <code>/warzone kits</code></td><td>Current kit or configured kit browser.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone items</code></td><td>Current item/ability restrictions.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone next</code></td><td>Next automatic ruleset.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone schedule</code></td><td>Rotation schedule.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/warzone help</code></td><td>Warzone command help.</td></tr></table><h2>Death Duels</h2><table><tr><td><code>/duel &lt;player&gt;</code></td><td>Build/send a duel challenge.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel review</code></td><td>Review incoming rules.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel accept</code> / <code>/duel deny</code></td><td>Accept or deny the reviewed challenge.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel info</code> / <code>/duel settings</code></td><td>Show active duel rules.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel draw</code> / <code>/draw</code></td><td>Request a mutual draw.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel surrender</code> / <code>/surrender</code></td><td>Currently also a mutual draw request, not an instant forfeit.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel cancel</code></td><td>Cancel queued flow; in an active duel, use draw/cancel handling.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/vault</code> / <code>/duel vault</code> / <code>/duelvault</code> / <code>/spoils</code> / <code>/claimspoils</code></td><td>Open victor's spoils.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/stats</code> / <code>/duel stats</code></td><td>Duel stats where your permission allows it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/duel watch</code> / <code>/duel spectate</code></td><td>Controlled duel spectating where your rank has the spectator permission.</td></tr></table><h2>AutoClicker</h2><table><tr><td><code>/autoclick</code></td><td>Toggle normal cooldown-based hostile-mob attacks.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/autoclick &lt;ticks&gt;</code></td><td>Fixed attempt interval.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/autoclick off</code> / <code>stop</code> / <code>disable</code></td><td>Stop it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/autoclick status</code></td><td>Show current AutoClicker mode.</td></tr></table><h2>Voting, trivia and giveaways</h2><table><tr><td><code>/vote</code></td><td>Open/show voting.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/votesites</code></td><td>Show individual vote sites.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/trivia stats</code></td><td>Your trivia stats.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/trivia top</code></td><td>Trivia leaderboard.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/giveaway</code></td><td>Open/enter the active giveaway.</td></tr></table><h2>Small utility commands</h2><table><tr><td><code>/sit</code></td><td>Sit using the server's sitting feature.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/lay</code></td><td>Lay down using the server's pose feature.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/offhand</code></td><td>Offhand utility command exposed to the player command set; use its in-game syntax for the exact action supported by the current utility plugin.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/jukebox</code></td><td>Jukebox/music utility command where your current rank has access.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/invisibleitemframes</code> / <code>/itf</code></td><td>Invisible-item-frame utility where your rank/feature access allows it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/scoreboard</code> / <code>/sb</code></td><td>Scoreboard controls/toggle provided by the current server setup.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/mail</code></td><td>Player-mail command root provided by the current server setup.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/bounty</code></td><td>Bounty-system command root where that feature is available.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/casino</code> / <code>/spin</code></td><td>Casino/spin feature roots where your current permission allows access.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/fastercrystals</code></td><td>Crystal-related player setting exposed by the current server setup.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/enthusiadonors</code></td><td>Donor/supporter feature command root.</td></tr></table><h2>Currently unavailable or not ordinary-player features</h2><table><tr><td><code>/event</code> / <code>/events</code></td><td>The custom Server Events system is in development and not enabled right now.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/startkoth</code></td><td>KOTH is currently disabled.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/gmc</code></td><td>Whitelisted command root but still permission-controlled; not documented as an ordinary player feature.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/tps</code></td><td>Whitelisted root but may be permission-controlled by the server performance command provider.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/velocity.hub</code></td><td>Proxy/network compatibility root; use <code>/hub</code> for normal player navigation.</td></tr></table><p>If a root is whitelisted but your rank does not have the underlying feature permission, the whitelist does not grant that permission by itself.</p>`}
});